Z||000007||BAM-BAM||06-05-2000||12:04 PM||||    Thanks guys, I'll have to look at the Grand Prix site. As for my GP, it's a 95SE 3.1L. The darn thing runs fine till it get's up to temp then the Cruise, speedo, HUD, and tranny drop out. My inclination is towards the Vehical Speed Sensor, but with the computer to computer to computer interfacing that these newer cars have, who knows. All the manuals defer you to the dealership  for any thing beyond basic troubleshooting and replacement. They enven defer half of that. I don't mind the hunt and peck meathod with my Fiero but my Grand Prix is the primary family transportation. Can't afford to leave it down to long, 5 people do not fit so well into an 85GT <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Well anyway, thanks again.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||87GT||06-05-2000||12:29 PM||||I bought a 94 Grand Prix SE 2-dr back in 1997 from a dealership and the same thing happened about a week after I bought it.  The alternator went south on me.  I was pretty pissed about it myself.  After I got that takin care of, it turned out to be a great car.  The 3.1 was a bit sluggish when I hit the gas when doing 65+ though.  Anyways, I sold my Grand Prix so that I could get my little 87GT outside.  Consumer Reports says the Grand Prix is unreliable but, from experience, I was happy with mine. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Flash Box||06-05-2000||12:33 PM||||Paul88GT,<BR>I agree with you on the 3rd gen site some of the members are rude but it is mostly the new members that have ruined the board being a Camaro/Firebird board it attracts younger people that are going to get one when they get their driver's license. <BR>(On a side note it is CAMARO not Camero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I am not tring to cut you or start a flame but The Camaro has always been my car and it just bugs me when I see it spelled that way.)<BR>I have found that I have been spending more time here on this site than others and it is due mostly to the people that are part of it.<BR>On that note I will just have to  Congratulate Cliff on a terrific site.||||reg||12
